IMPORT prelude

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 5), Parts II and III: the radio spectrum
-- plan, the radio frequency band plan and spectrum rights (regulations 3 to 18), in the 2002 Revised Edition.
-- Text: subjects/sg/telecommunications-radio-communication-regulations-2001/registers/source-bundle/TA1999-RG5.txt.
-- The Authority is the actor in most of these regulations; each rule here answers what the regulation lets the Authority do,
-- or what it requires of a holder or applicant, from facts the person or the Authority could state.
-- Amendments: S 707/2005 changes reg 16 (see sgta-i-rg5-amendments.l4); the other amending instruments do not touch Parts II and III.

§ `Rg 5 regulation 3: radio spectrum plans`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:291 | 3. —(1) The Authority may prepare and publish for information a radio spectrum plan
-- src:TA1999-RG5:292 | in any form as it considers appropriate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:293 | (2) A radio spectrum plan shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:294 | (a) conform with the Radio Regulations;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:295 | (b) have regard to any agreement, treaty or convention between Singapore and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:296 | any other country, in relation to radio frequency band planning and radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5:297 | emission;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:298 | (c) divide into such number of radio frequency bands as the Authority considers
-- src:TA1999-RG5:299 | appropriate so much of the radio spectrum as the Authority considers necessary
-- src:TA1999-RG5:300 | for the purpose of regulating radio-communication; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:301 | (d) specify the general purpose for which each radio frequency band may be used.
@ref Rg 5 reg 3 (src:TA1999-RG5:291-301)
GIVEN `it conforms with the Radio Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has regard to any agreement, treaty or convention between Singapore and another country on radio frequency band planning and radio emission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it divides into radio frequency bands so much of the radio spectrum as the Authority considers necessary for regulating radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it specifies the general purpose for which each radio frequency band may be used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 3(2): the radio spectrum plan has what the regulation requires of it` MEANS
        `it conforms with the Radio Regulations`
    AND `it has regard to any agreement, treaty or convention between Singapore and another country on radio frequency band planning and radio emission`
    AND `it divides into radio frequency bands so much of the radio spectrum as the Authority considers necessary for regulating radio-communication`
    AND `it specifies the general purpose for which each radio frequency band may be used`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 4: radio frequency band plans`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:303 | 4. —(1) The Authority may prepare and publish for information a radio frequency band
-- src:TA1999-RG5:304 | plan in any form as it considers appropriate relating to one or more radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5:305 | bands.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:306 | (2) A radio frequency band plan shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:307 | (a) be consistent with the use of the radio frequency bands specified in the radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5:308 | spectrum plan;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:309 | (b) conform with any applicable radio frequency band allocation plans made
-- src:TA1999-RG5:310 | pursuant to any agreement, treaty or convention which is binding on Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:311 | and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:312 | (c) specify the purpose for which the radio frequency band may be used.
@ref Rg 5 reg 4 (src:TA1999-RG5:303-312)
GIVEN `it is consistent with the use of the radio frequency bands specified in the radio spectrum plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it conforms with the radio frequency band allocation plans made under an agreement, treaty or convention binding on Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it specifies the purpose for which the radio frequency band may be used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 4(2): the radio frequency band plan has what the regulation requires of it` MEANS
        `it is consistent with the use of the radio frequency bands specified in the radio spectrum plan`
    AND `it conforms with the radio frequency band allocation plans made under an agreement, treaty or convention binding on Singapore`
    AND `it specifies the purpose for which the radio frequency band may be used`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 5: variation or revocation of the plans`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:315 | 5. The Authority may vary or revoke any radio spectrum plan or radio frequency band
-- src:TA1999-RG5:316 | plan, in whole or in part.
@ref Rg 5 reg 5 (src:TA1999-RG5:315-316)
GIVEN `the document is a radio spectrum plan or a radio frequency band plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 5: the Authority may vary or revoke the plan, in whole or in part` MEANS
    `the document is a radio spectrum plan or a radio frequency band plan`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 6: allocation of spectrum rights`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:325 | 6. —(1) The Authority may determine that any specified part of the radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5:326 | spectrum shall be allocated for use by persons by the grant of spectrum rights, but subject
-- src:TA1999-RG5:327 | to such restrictions as the Authority considers appropriate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:328 | (2) Subject to this Part, the Authority may, upon payment of the charges determined by
-- src:TA1999-RG5:329 | the Authority, grant any person the right to use any specified part of the radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5:330 | spectrum referred to in paragraph (1) for such period as it may specify.
@ref Rg 5 reg 6 (src:TA1999-RG5:325-330)
GIVEN `the Authority has determined that the specified part of the spectrum is allocated by the grant of spectrum rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charges the Authority determined have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 6(2): the Authority may grant the person a right to use the specified part of the spectrum` MEANS
        `the Authority has determined that the specified part of the spectrum is allocated by the grant of spectrum rights`
    AND `the charges the Authority determined have been paid`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 7: procedures for allocating spectrum rights`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:333 | 7. The procedure for allocating spectrum rights, the conditions for participation in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:334 | allocation of spectrum rights and the charges payable for spectrum rights shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG5:335 | determined by the Authority and, without limiting the methods which may be used, may
-- src:TA1999-RG5:336 | include any one or a combination of the following methods:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:337 | (a) by auction;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:338 | (b) by tender; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:339 | (c) by allocation for a pre-determined fee or a negotiated fee.
@ref Rg 5 reg 7 (src:TA1999-RG5:333-339)
GIVEN method IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 7: this is a method of allocation the regulation names` MEANS
    elem method (LIST "auction", "tender", "allocation for a pre-determined fee", "allocation for a negotiated fee")

§ `Rg 5 regulation 8: allocation subject to requirements`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:341 | 8. The Authority may refuse to grant any spectrum right to any person unless the person
-- src:TA1999-RG5:342 | meets such requirements as the Authority may determine.
@ref Rg 5 reg 8 (src:TA1999-RG5:341-342)
GIVEN `the person meets the requirements the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 8: the Authority may refuse to grant the person a spectrum right` MEANS
    (NOT `the person meets the requirements the Authority determined`)

§ `Rg 5 regulation 9: exclusion from allocation`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:345 | 9. —(1) The Authority may, by notice in writing, exclude any person from participating
-- src:TA1999-RG5:346 | or limit any person’s participation in the allocation of any spectrum right —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:347 | (a) for the purpose of developing the communications industry in Singapore and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:348 | maintaining effective competition between person engages in the provision of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:349 | radio-communication services; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:350 | (b) in the public interest.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:351 | (2) Before excluding any person from participating, or limiting any person’s
-- src:TA1999-RG5:352 | participation, in the allocation of any spectrum right, the Authority shall give the affected
-- src:TA1999-RG5:353 | person an opportunity to be heard.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:354 | (3) Any person aggrieved by the Authority’s decision under this regulation to exclude
-- src:TA1999-RG5:355 | any person from obtaining, or limit any person’s right to obtain, any spectrum right may
-- src:TA1999-RG5:356 | appeal to the Minister whose decision shall be final.
@ref Rg 5 reg 9 (src:TA1999-RG5:345-356)
GIVEN `the purpose is developing the communications industry in Singapore and maintaining effective competition between providers of radio-communication services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 9(1): the Authority may by written notice exclude or limit the person's participation in the allocation` MEANS
    `the purpose is developing the communications industry in Singapore and maintaining effective competition between providers of radio-communication services`
    OR `it is in the public interest`

GIVEN `the Authority gave the affected person an opportunity to be heard first` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 9(2): the exclusion or limit was made as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the Authority gave the affected person an opportunity to be heard first`

GIVEN `the person is aggrieved by the decision under regulation 9 to exclude or limit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 9(3): the person may appeal to the Minister, whose decision is final` MEANS
    `the person is aggrieved by the decision under regulation 9 to exclude or limit`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 10: conditions of grant of spectrum rights`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:359 | 10. A spectrum right granted by the Authority shall be subject to such conditions as the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:360 | Authority considers appropriate, including —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:361 | (a) conditions specifying the part or parts of the radio frequency spectrum in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:362 | which the operation of a station or network is authorised;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:363 | (b) conditions specifying the type of station or network, and type of equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG5:364 | comprising the station or network, which the person granted the spectrum right is
-- src:TA1999-RG5:365 | authorised to operate;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:366 | (c) conditions specifying the periods during which operation of a station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:367 | network is authorised;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:368 | (d) conditions specifying that the person granted the spectrum right and persons
-- src:TA1999-RG5:369 | authorised by that person to operate a station or network shall not operate any
-- src:TA1999-RG5:370 | station or network without a station (spectrum) licence or a network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:371 | licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:372 | (e) conditions specifying the maximum permitted level of radio emission, that
-- src:TA1999-RG5:373 | may be caused by operation of a station or network under the licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:374 | (f) conditions specifying the area within which operation of a station or network is
-- src:TA1999-RG5:375 | authorised;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:376 | (g) conditions specifying the maximum permitted level of radio emission, outside
-- src:TA1999-RG5:377 | the area referred to in paragraph (f), that may be caused by the operation of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:378 | station or network;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:379 | (h) conditions requiring the payment to the Authority of the charges for the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:380 | spectrum right determined by the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:381 | (i) conditions requiring the person granted the spectrum right to comply with the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:382 | directions of the Authority concerning the use of the spectrum right; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:383 | (j) such other conditions as the Authority considers appropriate.
@ref Rg 5 reg 10 (src:TA1999-RG5:359-383)
GIVEN `kind of condition` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 10: this is a kind of condition the regulation names for a spectrum right` MEANS
    elem `kind of condition` (LIST "the part of the spectrum in which operation is authorised"
                                 , "the type of station or network and its equipment"
                                 , "the periods during which operation is authorised"
                                 , "no operation without a station (spectrum) licence or a network (spectrum) licence"
                                 , "the maximum level of radio emission"
                                 , "the area within which operation is authorised"
                                 , "the maximum level of radio emission outside that area"
                                 , "payment of the charges for the spectrum right"
                                 , "compliance with the Authority's directions on the use of the right"
                                 , "such other conditions as the Authority considers appropriate")

§ `Rg 5 regulation 11: authorisation to use the assigned spectrum`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:386 | 11. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), a spectrum right authorises —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:387 | (a) the person granted the spectrum right; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:388 | (b) if the conditions of the grant of spectrum right permit, any person authorised
-- src:TA1999-RG5:389 | by the person granted the spectrum right,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:390 | to use the assigned radio frequency spectrum, in accordance with the conditions of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:391 | grant, for the purpose of operating a station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:392 | (2) Except as may be permitted by the Authority, a person is not authorised to operate a
-- src:TA1999-RG5:393 | station or network under paragraph (1) unless the person has, and complies with the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:394 | conditions of, a station (spectrum) licence or a network (spectrum) licence, as the case
-- src:TA1999-RG5:395 | may be.
@ref Rg 5 reg 11 (src:TA1999-RG5:386-395)
GIVEN `the person was granted the spectrum right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions of the grant permit it, and the person was authorised by the person granted the right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 11(1): the person is authorised to use the assigned spectrum for operating a station or network` MEANS
    `the person was granted the spectrum right` OR `the conditions of the grant permit it, and the person was authorised by the person granted the right`

GIVEN `the person has, and complies with the conditions of, a station (spectrum) licence or a network (spectrum) licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority permitted the operation without one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 11(2): the person is authorised to operate the station or network` MEANS
    `the person has, and complies with the conditions of, a station (spectrum) licence or a network (spectrum) licence` OR `the Authority permitted the operation without one`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 12: spectrum sharing`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:401 | 12. —(1) Subject to such conditions as the Authority may generally or specifically
-- src:TA1999-RG5:402 | impose, a person granted a spectrum right may authorise another person to use the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:403 | assigned radio frequency spectrum, in accordance with the conditions of the grant, for the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:404 | purpose of operating a station or network subject to that person obtaining a station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:405 | (spectrum) licence or a network (spectrum) licence, as the case may be.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:406 | (2) Any person authorised by a person granted a spectrum right to use the assigned radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5:407 | frequency spectrum under paragraph (1) shall comply with the Act, these Regulations and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:408 | such other requirements as the Authority may specify.
@ref Rg 5 reg 12 (src:TA1999-RG5:401-408)
GIVEN `the person granted the spectrum right authorised the other person, within the conditions of the grant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person obtained the station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum) licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 12(1): the other person may use the assigned spectrum to operate a station or network` MEANS
    `the person granted the spectrum right authorised the other person, within the conditions of the grant` AND `the other person obtained the station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum) licence`

GIVEN `the person complies with the Act, these Regulations and the other requirements the Authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 12(2): the authorised person is meeting what the regulation requires of the person` MEANS
    `the person complies with the Act, these Regulations and the other requirements the Authority specified`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 13: spectrum trading`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:411 | 13. —(1) Subject to such conditions as the Authority may generally or specifically
-- src:TA1999-RG5:412 | impose, a person granted a spectrum right may assign, or otherwise deal with, the whole
-- src:TA1999-RG5:413 | or any part of the rights and privileges granted under the spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:414 | (2) No assignment of or dealing with the whole or any part of the rights and privileges
-- src:TA1999-RG5:415 | granted under a spectrum right shall take effect until the Authority gives its approval in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:416 | writing.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:417 | (3) The parties to an assignment of or dealing with the whole or any part of the rights
-- src:TA1999-RG5:418 | and privileges granted under a spectrum right must give to the Authority such
-- src:TA1999-RG5:419 | information about the assignment or dealing as the Authority requires for the purpose of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:420 | giving its approval under paragraph (2).
@ref Rg 5 reg 13 (src:TA1999-RG5:411-420)
GIVEN `the assignment or dealing is within the conditions the Authority imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 13(1): the person granted the spectrum right may assign or deal with the rights and privileges` MEANS
    `the assignment or dealing is within the conditions the Authority imposed`

GIVEN `the Authority has given its approval in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 13(2): the assignment or dealing takes effect` MEANS
    `the Authority has given its approval in writing`

GIVEN `the parties gave the Authority the information it requires for the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 13(3): the parties have done what the regulation requires of them` MEANS
    `the parties gave the Authority the information it requires for the approval`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 14: variation of conditions upon assignment`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:422 | 14. The Authority may do any one or more of the following if it is satisfied that it is
-- src:TA1999-RG5:423 | necessary or convenient to do so in order to give effect to any assignment or dealing
-- src:TA1999-RG5:424 | under regulation 13:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:425 | (a) vary a spectrum right by changing the name of the person to whom the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:426 | spectrum right was granted;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:427 | (b) vary the conditions of grant of a spectrum right by —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:428 | (i) including one or more further conditions; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:429 | (ii) revoking or varying any condition;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:430 | (c) issue one or more new spectrum rights; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:431 | (d) cancel one or more existing spectrum rights.
@ref Rg 5 reg 14 (src:TA1999-RG5:422-431)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied it is necessary or convenient to give effect to an assignment or dealing under regulation 13` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 14: the Authority may vary, issue or cancel spectrum rights to give effect to the assignment or dealing` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied it is necessary or convenient to give effect to an assignment or dealing under regulation 13`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 15: variation of certain conditions`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:438 | 15. —(1) Subject to this regulation, the Authority may vary any condition of any grant
-- src:TA1999-RG5:439 | of a spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:440 | (2) This regulation shall not apply to a resumption of any spectrum right under
-- src:TA1999-RG5:441 | regulation 17 or 18 or to a variation of the conditions of any grant of a spectrum right
-- src:TA1999-RG5:442 | under regulation 14 or 17 (3).
-- src:TA1999-RG5:443 | (3) Before varying the conditions of any grant of a spectrum right under this regulation,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:444 | the Authority shall give notice to the person granted the spectrum right —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:445 | (a) stating that it proposes to make the variations in the manner as specified in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:446 | notice; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:447 | (b) specifying the time (not being less than 28 days from the date of service of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:448 | notice) within which written representations with respect to the proposed variation
-- src:TA1999-RG5:449 | may be made.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:450 | (4) Upon receipt of any written representation referred to in paragraph (3), the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5:451 | shall consider the representation and may —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:452 | (a) reject the representation; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:453 | (b) amend the proposed variation in accordance with the representation, or in any
-- src:TA1999-RG5:454 | manner as the Authority considers appropriate,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:455 | and, in either event, the Authority shall issue a direction in writing to the person granted
-- src:TA1999-RG5:456 | the spectrum right requiring that effect be given to the proposed variation specified in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:457 | notice or to the variation as amended by the Authority within a reasonable time.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:458 | (5) Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Authority under paragraph (4) may,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:459 | within 14 days of the receipt of the direction, appeal to the Minister whose decision shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5:460 | be final.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:461 | (6) The Authority shall not enforce its direction —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:462 | (a) during the period referred to in paragraph (5); and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:463 | (b) whilst the appeal is under consideration by the Minister.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:464 | (7) If no written representation is received by the Authority within the time specified in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:465 | paragraph (3) or if any written representation made under that paragraph is subsequently
-- src:TA1999-RG5:466 | withdrawn, the Authority may forthwith carry out the variation as specified in the notice
-- src:TA1999-RG5:467 | given under that paragraph.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:468 | (8) Notwithstanding paragraphs (3) to (7), the Authority may, with the agreement of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:469 | person granted the spectrum right, vary the conditions of any spectrum right in such
-- src:TA1999-RG5:470 | manner as may be agreed.
@ref Rg 5 reg 15 (src:TA1999-RG5:438-470)
GIVEN `it is a resumption under regulation 17 or 18, or a variation under regulation 14 or 17(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 15(1) and (2): the regulation applies to the variation` MEANS
    (NOT `it is a resumption under regulation 17 or 18, or a variation under regulation 14 or 17(3)`)

GIVEN `days from the date of service of the notice to the time for written representations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 15(3): the time allowed for written representations is long enough` MEANS
    `days from the date of service of the notice to the time for written representations` AT LEAST 28

GIVEN `days from receipt of the direction to the appeal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 15(5): the appeal to the Minister is within time` MEANS
    `days from receipt of the direction to the appeal` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `within the 14 days to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is under consideration by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 15(6): the Authority may enforce its direction` MEANS
    (NOT `within the 14 days to appeal`) AND (NOT `the appeal is under consideration by the Minister`)

GIVEN `no written representation was received in time, or any representation was withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person granted the spectrum right agrees to the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 15(7) and (8): the Authority may carry out the variation at once` MEANS
    `no written representation was received in time, or any representation was withdrawn` OR `the person granted the spectrum right agrees to the variation`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 16: suspension or cancellation of spectrum rights`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:473 | 16. —(1) The Authority may suspend or cancel the grant of any spectrum right, or a part
-- src:TA1999-RG5:474 | of a spectrum right, if the Authority is satisfied that —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:475 | (a) the grant of the spectrum right was obtained by fraud or misrepresentation; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:476 | (b) the person to whom the spectrum right is granted, is contravening, or has
-- src:TA1999-RG5:477 | contravened —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:478 | (i) any of the provisions of the Act or these Regulations;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:479 | (ii) any condition of the grant of the spectrum right; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:480 | (iii) any direction given to the person by the Authority under the Act or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:481 | these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:482 | (2) The Authority, before suspending or cancelling the grant of any spectrum right, shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5:483 | give to the person to whom the spectrum right was granted notice in writing of its
-- src:TA1999-RG5:484 | intention to do so and shall in such notice call upon that person to show cause within such
-- src:TA1999-RG5:485 | time as may be specified in the notice as to why the person’s spectrum right should not be
-- src:TA1999-RG5:486 | suspended or cancelled.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:487 | (3) If the person to whom a notice has been given under subsection (2) —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:488 | (a) fails to show cause within the period of time given to him to do so or such
-- src:TA1999-RG5:489 | extended period of time as the Authority may allow; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:490 | (b) fails to show sufficient cause,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:491 | the Authority shall give notice in writing to that person of the date from which the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:492 | suspension or cancellation of the person’s spectrum right, as the case may be, is to take
-- src:TA1999-RG5:493 | effect.
@ref Rg 5 reg 16 (src:TA1999-RG5:473-493)
GIVEN `the grant was obtained by fraud or misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is contravening, or has contravened, the Act or these Regulations, a condition of the grant, or a direction of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 16(1): the Authority may suspend or cancel the spectrum right, in whole or in part` MEANS
    `the grant was obtained by fraud or misrepresentation`
    OR `the person is contravening, or has contravened, the Act or these Regulations, a condition of the grant, or a direction of the Authority`

GIVEN `the Authority gave written notice of its intention, calling on the person to show cause within a time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to show cause in time, or failed to show sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 16(2) and (3): the Authority may give notice of the date the suspension or cancellation takes effect` MEANS
    `the Authority gave written notice of its intention, calling on the person to show cause within a time` AND `the person failed to show cause in time, or failed to show sufficient cause`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 17: resumption of spectrum rights by agreement`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:496 | 17. —(1) The Authority may resume a spectrum right, or a part of a spectrum right,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:497 | under an agreement entered into with the person granted the spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:498 | (2) Without limiting the matters that may be included in the agreement, if a part of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:499 | spectrum right is to be resumed, the agreement must specify the variations to the other
-- src:TA1999-RG5:500 | conditions of the spectrum right that will be made to give effect to the agreement and the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:501 | date on which the resumption is to take effect.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:502 | (3) If a part of the spectrum right is resumed, the Authority shall vary, in a way that
-- src:TA1999-RG5:503 | gives effect to the variations specified in the agreement, the other conditions of the grant
-- src:TA1999-RG5:504 | of spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:505 | (4) For the purposes of this regulation and regulation 18, “resume”, in relation to a grant
-- src:TA1999-RG5:506 | of any spectrum right or part of a spectrum right, means to revoke or vary any condition
-- src:TA1999-RG5:507 | relating to —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:508 | (a) the range of the radio frequencies comprised in the grant of the spectrum right;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:509 | (b) the duration of the grant of the spectrum right; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:510 | (c) the geographical area covered by the grant of the spectrum right.
@ref Rg 5 reg 17 (src:TA1999-RG5:496-510)
GIVEN `there is an agreement with the person granted the spectrum right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 17(1): the Authority may resume the spectrum right, or a part of it` MEANS
    `there is an agreement with the person granted the spectrum right`

GIVEN `the agreement specifies the variations to the other conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement specifies the date on which the resumption takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 17(2): an agreement to resume a part of the right has the contents the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the agreement specifies the variations to the other conditions` AND `the agreement specifies the date on which the resumption takes effect`

GIVEN `the change revokes or varies a condition on the range of radio frequencies, the duration of the grant, or the geographical area covered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 17(4): the change is a resumption` MEANS
    `the change revokes or varies a condition on the range of radio frequencies, the duration of the grant, or the geographical area covered`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 18: resumption of spectrum rights compulsorily`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:513 | 18. —(1) Subject to this regulation, the Authority may resume a spectrum right, or a part
-- src:TA1999-RG5:514 | of a spectrum right, without the agreement of the person granted the spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:515 | (2) The Authority may only resume a spectrum right or a part of a spectrum right
-- src:TA1999-RG5:516 | without agreement of the person granted the spectrum right if the Minister has approved
-- src:TA1999-RG5:517 | the resumption by notification published in the Gazette.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:518 | (3) Before resuming a spectrum right or a part of a spectrum right under this regulation,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:519 | the Authority shall give notice to the person granted the spectrum right —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:520 | (a) stating that it proposes to resume the spectrum right or a part of the spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5:521 | right in the manner specified in the notice and the compensation payable for the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:522 | resumption;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:523 | (b) specifying the time (not being less than 28 days from the date of service of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:524 | notice) within which written representations on the proposed resumption may be
-- src:TA1999-RG5:525 | made; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:526 | (c) if applicable, specifying the variations to the other conditions of the spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5:527 | right that will be made to give effect to the resumption.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:528 | (4) Upon receipt of any written representation referred to in paragraph (3), the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5:529 | shall consider the representation and may —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:530 | (a) reject the representation; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:531 | (b) amend the proposed resumption, the compensation payable and the variations
-- src:TA1999-RG5:532 | to the other conditions of the spectrum right, in accordance with the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:533 | representation, or in any other manner as the Authority considers appropriate,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:534 | and, in either event, the Authority shall issue a direction in writing to the person granted
-- src:TA1999-RG5:535 | the spectrum right requiring that effect be given to the proposed resumption specified in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:536 | the notice or to the resumption as subsequently amended by the Authority within a
-- src:TA1999-RG5:537 | reasonable time.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:538 | (5) Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Authority under paragraph (4) may,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:539 | within 14 days of the receipt of the direction, appeal to the Minister whose decision shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5:540 | be final.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:541 | (6) The Authority shall not enforce its direction —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:542 | (a) during the period referred to in paragraph (5); and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:543 | (b) whilst the appeal is under consideration by the Minister.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:544 | (7) If no written representation is received by the Authority within the time specified in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:545 | paragraph (3) or if any written representation made under that paragraph is subsequently
-- src:TA1999-RG5:546 | withdrawn, the Authority may forthwith carry out the resumption as specified in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:547 | notice given under that paragraph.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:548 | (8) Regulation 15 shall not apply to the variations to the other conditions of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:549 | spectrum right made under this regulation.
@ref Rg 5 reg 18 (src:TA1999-RG5:513-549)
GIVEN `the Minister approved the resumption by notification published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 18(1) and (2): the Authority may resume the spectrum right without the agreement of the person granted it` MEANS
    `the Minister approved the resumption by notification published in the Gazette`

GIVEN `days from the date of service of the notice to the time for written representations` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice states the proposed resumption and the compensation payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 18(3): the notice of resumption is as the regulation requires` MEANS
    (`days from the date of service of the notice to the time for written representations` AT LEAST 28)
    AND `the notice states the proposed resumption and the compensation payable`

GIVEN `days from receipt of the direction to the appeal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 18(5): the appeal to the Minister is within time` MEANS
    `days from receipt of the direction to the appeal` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `within the 14 days to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is under consideration by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 18(6): the Authority may enforce its direction` MEANS
    (NOT `within the 14 days to appeal`) AND (NOT `the appeal is under consideration by the Minister`)

GIVEN `no written representation was received in time, or any representation was withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 18(7): the Authority may carry out the resumption at once` MEANS
    `no written representation was received in time, or any representation was withdrawn`

GIVEN `the variation is made under regulation 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 18(8): regulation 15 applies to the variation of the other conditions` MEANS
    (NOT `the variation is made under regulation 18`)
